# The gcc driver on CuBit (userspace/ports/gcc): what userspace/libc/cubit-cc
# passes, as specs, installed as toolchain/lib/gcc/x86_64-linux-musl/15.3.0/specs
# where the driver reads it. Programs are static, non-PIE ELF linked with
# the libc's script (cubit.ld) and a 1 MiB stack contract (a later
# -Wl,-z,stack-size=N overrides it); the start code is cubit-crt1.o, then
# gcc's static init/fini frame. ld links directly: no collect2, no LTO
# (decision D4).

*cc1:
+ -mno-red-zone

*startfile:
cubit-crt1.o%s crti.o%s crtbeginT.o%s

*endfile:
crtend.o%s crtn.o%s

*link:
-m elf_x86_64 -static -T cubit.ld%s -z stack-size=1048576 -z noexecstack -z noseparate-code

*lib:
-lc

*libgcc:
-lgcc

*link_gcc_c_sequence:
--start-group %G %L --end-group

*linker:
ld

